  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Mental Health and Trauma Resilience Development amongst Israeli, Palestinian and European Youth.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Danish and Palestinian Youth Leaders will create a cross-border, inter-ethnic and religious pragmatic and academic database equipped to respond to psychological needs for local and European youth in reconciliation. Currently, Palestinian and Israeli youth is surviving through trauma, grief, and despair as violence, insecurity, unsafety, hopelessness cause unseen mental and emotional suffering. Both Israeli and Palestinian youth&apos;s well-being is harmed by dehumanization, existential fear, hatred, and victimization. To respond adequately to these psychological obstacles to reconciliation and peacebuilding, Musalaha will coordinate a taskforce of exemplary Youth Leaders that will map out the needs, responses, and organize dissemination events.</narrative>
  </description>
